                                      | kernel alt    -0.99627    0.0037          3.89   residual matter 55.1x less than Newtonian
        20   -3.283715e-02     -2.613 |  Newtonian    -0.79470    0.2053           nan
                                      | kernel can    -0.99219    0.0078          3.15   residual matter 26.3x less than Newtonian
                                      | kernel alt    -0.99411    0.0059          3.43   residual matter 34.8x less than Newtonian
        30   -3.283715e-02     -2.613 |  Newtonian    -0.79470    0.2053           nan
                                      | kernel can    -0.98619    0.0138          2.61   residual matter 14.9x less than Newtonian
                                      | kernel alt    -0.98929    0.0107          2.85   residual matter 19.2x less than Newtonian

    across all radii and both footings the kernel leaves between 14.9x and 164.8x less residual matter
    the kernel branch reaches shell crossing at z = 2.6 to 5.1, against z = 0 for the Newtonian branch by construction
  [PASS] V4 [THE FRONT HAS TEETH -- THE TWO BRANCHES ARE NOT DEGENERATE] with the initial condition fixed by the Newtonian branch matching the observed void, the kernel branch is run from the same initial condition and the residual matter fraction 1+delta is compared; a ratio above 3 means the prediction is separable from LCDM by any measurement of void emptiness
           (the kernel leaves 14.9x to 164.8x less residual matter than Newtonian from an identical initial under-density, and drives shell crossing forward from z = 0 to z = 2.6-5.1. Against the threshold 3 this is a large, separable effect -- IN BRANCH (ii) ONLY; branch (i) is Newtonian by construction and predicts the Newtonian column exactly)

================================================================================================================
V5 -- confrontation with the observed void density profile
================================================================================================================
    THE THRESHOLD, STATED SEPARATELY AND BEFORE THE MEASUREMENT.  Stacked void profiles
    (Hamaus+2014 PRL 112 251302; Ricciardelli+2014 MNRAS 440 601; Nadathur+2015 MNRAS 449
    3997; Hamaus+2016 JCAP 11 018) find central TRACER contrast about -0.8 for large voids;
    the MEAN interior matter contrast that corresponds to is shallower than the central value
    and carries tracer-bias and void-finder systematics in both directions.  The envelope
    adopted here is deliberately GENEROUS to the framework: residual matter fraction
    1+delta_bar between 0.1 and 0.5 (i.e. delta_bar between -0.90 and -0.50).
    A branch is in tension only if it falls BELOW the floor, i.e. empties voids further than
    the most extreme reading of the data allows.

    Newtonian branch  : 1+delta_bar = 0.2053  -- inside the envelope BY CONSTRUCTION (it was calibrated there)
    kernel branch (ii): 1+delta_bar = 0.00125 to 0.01381 across radii and footings
    the kernel therefore leaves 15x to 165x less matter in a void than the observations accommodate
  [PASS] V5 [THE KERNEL BRANCH OVER-EMPTIES VOIDS PAST THE MOST GENEROUS READING OF THE DATA] the residual matter fraction the kernel branch leaves inside a void is compared with a floor set in advance from the published stacked void profiles and deliberately widened in the framework's favour; falling below that floor in EVERY case is the tension
           (the least-emptied kernel case over all radii and both footings is 1+delta_bar = 0.01381, against the generous floor 0.1: a factor 7 below it, and a factor 15 below the calibrated Newtonian value. This reproduces and generalises stage53 C2(ii)'s single number -0.993 across the observed size range. IT IS NOT A KILL: see V8, and note the kernel branch is past shell crossing (V4) where the top-hat is an extrapolation, so the DIRECTION is robust and the VALUE is not)

================================================================================================================
V6 -- the void size function: which way, and roughly how much
================================================================================================================
    Sheth & van de Weygaert 2004 MNRAS 350 517: the void multiplicity carries the factor
    exp(-delta_v^2 / 2 sigma^2(R_L)), delta_v the LINEAR contrast at which the void reaches
    shell crossing.  A kernel that evacuates faster reaches shell crossing from a SHALLOWER
    initial under-density, so |delta_v| falls and the exponential rises: MORE voids, LARGER.
    sigma(R) is BBKS+Sugiyama normalised to sigma_8 = 0.811 -- the CMB-anchored linear
    amplitude, which both branches share at z = 100.

       R_L  sigma_L(R_L)   dv Newton  dv kernel can  dv kernel alt   N_M/N_N can          alt
         8        0.8110      -2.613        -0.000        -0.000     1.794e+02    1.794e+02
        12        0.6044      -2.613        -0.000        -0.000     1.144e+04    1.144e+04
        15        0.5057      -2.613        -0.000        -0.000     6.270e+05    6.270e+05
        20        0.3942      -2.613        -0.000        -0.000     3.481e+09    3.481e+09
        30        0.2665      -2.613        -0.000        -0.000     7.440e+20    7.440e+20

    NOTE: for 10 kernel-branch cases no seed as shallow as |delta_i| = 1e-13 at z = 100
    avoids shell crossing by z = 0 (the deep-MOND enhancement nu ~ (a_0/g)^(1/2) diverges as the
    peculiar field vanishes), so the kernel barrier |delta_v| is an UPPER BOUND (< 8e-13 in linear
    z = 0 units) and the exponential factor N_M/N_N is a LOWER BOUND, not a value.

    the kernel barrier is shallower than the Newtonian one at every radius and both footings;
    the largest ratio |delta_v,kernel| / |delta_v,Newton| is 0.000
    THE MAGNITUDE IS NOT A PREDICTION.  The exponential is the LEADING factor only, sigma(R_L)
    enters squared in a denominator, and the SvdW barrier is itself a spherical construction.
    Only the SIGN and the ordering are defensible from this calculation.
  [PASS] V6 [THE SIZE FUNCTION MOVES THE SAME WAY AT EVERY RADIUS: MORE AND LARGER VOIDS] the linear shell-crossing barrier is computed for both branches on the same integrator and the same CMB-anchored sigma(R); the kernel barrier must be shallower than the Newtonian barrier at every radius and both footings for the direction to be a clean prediction rather than a radius-dependent mixture
           (the deepest kernel barrier is 0.000 of the Newtonian one, threshold 1.0 -- shallower everywhere. The exponential factor that follows runs 1.8e+02 to 7.4e+20, which is quoted as a DIRECTION with an order of magnitude and must never be quoted as a predicted abundance)

================================================================================================================
V7 -- does the external field rescue it?  The one escape a MOND kernel always has
================================================================================================================
    A void is not isolated.  If the external field of surrounding structure exceeds the void's
    own internal field, the kernel is evaluated at the external value and the internal boost
    collapses.  This is the standard EFE escape and it must be tested, not assumed away.
    measured on the twelve real voids of V2: median g_ext / g_int = 1.29
    (range 0.36 to 2.68)
    ASSUMPTION, stated: this ratio is held constant over the void's history.  In linear
    theory both fields scale as a^-1 so the ratio is constant; once the void goes non-linear
    its own field saturates while the external one keeps growing, so the true late-time
    ratio is LARGER and the quench applied here is the CONSERVATIVE one.

       R_L    footing  y_int(z=0)  y_ext used  1+delta free  1+delta EFE
        12  canonical     0.00594     0.00766       0.00351      0.00391
        12        alt     0.00493     0.00636       0.00256      0.00285
        20  canonical     0.00990     0.01277       0.00781      0.00881
        20        alt     0.00822     0.01060       0.00589      0.00662

    the EFE quench raises the residual matter fraction to at most 0.00881, still a factor 11 below the generous floor 0.1
  [PASS] V7 [THE EXTERNAL FIELD DOES NOT RESCUE THE OVER-EMPTYING] the external-to-internal field ratio measured on real local voids is fed back into the kernel as a quasi-linear external-field term and the evacuation re-run; the over-emptying survives only if the residual matter fraction stays below the same floor used in V5
           (with the measured median quench g_ext/g_int = 1.29 applied throughout, the largest residual fraction reached is 0.00881 against the floor 0.1. The external field real voids sit in is far too weak to switch the kernel off, because the void's own field and its surroundings' field are BOTH far below a_0 -- which is the whole point of the environment. The EFE escape that rescues wide binaries and dwarf satellites is not available here)

================================================================================================================
V8 -- what this calculation cannot decide, quantified rather than asserted
================================================================================================================
    STATED PROMINENTLY.  (1) A spherical top-hat is a crude model of a void: real voids are
    aspherical, contain substructure, and the kernel branch is PAST SHELL CROSSING for most of
    its evolution (V4), where the top-hat is an extrapolation and not a solution.  (2) Void
    statistics depend strongly on the tracer and on the void-finder definition: watershed,
    spherical-underdensity and ZOBOV/VIDE finders return different central contrasts on the
    same field, and tracer bias converts between galaxy and matter contrast with an uncertainty
    that is itself density dependent.  NO KILL IS CLAIMED FROM A SPHERICAL MODEL.
    (3) The governing fork: the framework's OWN covariant cosmology has linear enhancement
    EXACTLY 1 (stage53 C2(i), item 85), in which case the Newtonian column IS the framework's
    prediction and this entire front is empty.

    what IS testable here is how far the branch-(ii) answer moves under the modelling choices
    that are actually free:
      nu_simple canonical R20          1+delta_bar = 0.01419
      nu_simple alt R20                1+delta_bar = 0.01069
      z_i = 30 canonical R20           1+delta_bar = 0.00927
      nu_RAR canonical R20             1+delta_bar = 0.00781
      nu_simple canonical R12          1+delta_bar = 0.00631
      nu_RAR alt R20                   1+delta_bar = 0.00589
      nu_simple alt R12                1+delta_bar = 0.00457
      z_i = 30 canonical R12           1+delta_bar = 0.00438
      nu_RAR canonical R12             1+delta_bar = 0.00351
      nu_RAR alt R12                   1+delta_bar = 0.00256
      a0~H(z) rival canonical R20      1+delta_bar = 0.00005
      a0~H(z) rival alt R20            1+delta_bar = 0.00004
      a0~H(z) rival canonical R12      1+delta_bar = 0.00002
      a0~H(z) rival alt R12            1+delta_bar = 0.00001

    the whole spread is 0.00001 to 0.01419; the floor is 0.1
  [PASS] V8 [THE DIRECTION SURVIVES EVERY MODELLING CHOICE THAT IS ACTUALLY FREE, WHICH IS NOT THE SAME AS SURVIVING THE MODEL] both kernels, both footings, two Lagrangian radii, two starting redshifts and the rival a_0 proportional to H(z) branch are run and the full spread of the residual matter fraction is compared with the same floor; the direction is robust only if the entire spread stays on one side of it
           (the whole spread 0.00001 to 0.01419 lies below the floor 0.1, so no choice among kernel, footing, radius, starting redshift or a_0(z) branch reverses the sign. The rival a_0 proportional to H(z) branch makes the over-emptying WORSE, not better, because a larger a_0 at early times pushes the void DEEPER into the MOND regime. What this does NOT establish is that the spherical model itself is adequate, and that is the limitation that actually binds)

================================================================================================================
WHAT THIS FRONT IS WORTH
================================================================================================================
    Branch (ii) 'MOND-on' makes a large, sign-definite, environment-proof prediction: voids
    empty to a residual matter fraction of order 1e-2 or less, reach shell crossing at
    z ~ 5, and the size function is pushed to more and larger voids.  That is
    in the wrong direction against every published void profile, and V7 shows the external
    field cannot switch it off.  But branch (ii) was ALREADY excluded in this repo on the
    KBC amplitude and on sigma_8 -> 1.38 (stage53 C2), so this is an INDEPENDENT CONFIRMATION
    of a known failure, not a new kill.
    Branch (i), the framework's own covariant cosmology, has linear enhancement exactly 1 and
    therefore predicts the Newtonian column -- no void signal at all.
    NET: cosmic voids are NOT a live discriminating front for this framework as it stands.
    They become one only if a covariant completion is found whose cosmological perturbations
    carry a MOND enhancement, and then voids would be among the sharpest tests available,
    because V7 shows the usual external-field escape is closed there.

